\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S13}{\ignorespaces Recovery on simulated sections, scaled to the simulated world: three worlds per planted spill-over fraction{}, each fitted with three model seeds; the range over the 9 fits of each row. NMI of $\bm  {\mu }_z$ with the planted type; \emph  {CCA}: first canonical correlation of $\bm  {\mu }_w$ with the planted response; \emph  {Loadings}: principal-angle cosine of the fitted against the planted loadings; \emph  {Comp.\ $R^2$}: within-type $R^2$ of neighbour composition from $\bm  {\mu }_z$. Bold: the matched $\kappa $. \emph  {References}: NMI of clusters of the counts and of the planted intrinsic state, composition $R^2$ of the planted state, and the loading cosine of a random subspace (mean and 95th percentile), each the range over the three worlds and both planted rates. A fit is stopped early on $15\%$ of held-out tiles; every read covers all cells. Arrows give the preferred direction.\relax }}{18}{table.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
